WEBVTT

00:00:00.281 --> 00:00:02.746
Last video stopped at one over x, where

00:00:02.766 --> 00:00:04.370
the power rule would divide by zero.

00:00:05.193 --> 00:00:06.078
Here's a rate like that.

00:00:06.743 --> 00:00:08.513
A fundraiser's donations slow down.

00:00:09.196 --> 00:00:11.060
On day t, they come in at a

00:00:11.202 --> 00:00:12.845
thousand over t dollars a day.

00:00:13.488 --> 00:00:15.841
So the total raised has gradient a thousand

00:00:15.902 --> 00:00:16.163
over t.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.696
The same term sits in this question:

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.629
two e to the three x, plus four

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:22.171
over x.

00:00:22.836 --> 00:00:24.666
The first term is done: two thirds e

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:25.612
to the three x.

00:00:26.238 --> 00:00:27.328
The second is still waiting.

00:00:28.037 --> 00:00:30.150
So which curve has a gradient of one

00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:30.794
over x?

00:00:31.539 --> 00:00:33.447
And why will the answer need the absolute

00:00:33.528 --> 00:00:36.179
value of x, often read as mod x?

00:00:36.795 --> 00:00:38.442
Think about what a primitive means here.

00:00:39.065 --> 00:00:41.410
We want a curve whose gradient, at each

00:00:41.752 --> 00:00:41.871
x,

00:00:42.413 --> 00:00:44.337
equals the height of one over x.

00:00:45.081 --> 00:00:46.868
For positive x, we already know one.

00:00:47.331 --> 00:00:49.036
The derivative of the natural log of x

00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:50.100
is one over x.

00:00:50.804 --> 00:00:53.208
At x equals two, the log curve has

00:00:53.249 --> 00:00:55.633
gradient one half, the same as the height

00:00:55.714 --> 00:00:56.916
of one over x at two.

00:00:57.679 --> 00:00:59.944
But one over x has a second piece

00:01:00.085 --> 00:01:01.809
on the left, where x is negative.

00:01:02.452 --> 00:01:04.181
The natural log of x doesn't exist there,

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:05.991
so it can't be the whole answer.

00:01:06.655 --> 00:01:08.778
On the left, one over x is negative,

00:01:09.219 --> 00:01:11.343
so the curve we want must go downhill

00:01:11.524 --> 00:01:12.505
as x increases.

00:01:13.228 --> 00:01:15.700
Near zero it must be steep, and further

00:01:15.722 --> 00:01:17.169
left it must flatten out.

00:01:17.894 --> 00:01:19.846
That's the log curve, mirrored in the y

00:01:19.928 --> 00:01:20.209
axis.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.721
Mirroring left to right reverses every slope.

00:01:24.323 --> 00:01:26.569
At x equals minus two, the mirrored curve

00:01:26.611 --> 00:01:29.338
has gradient minus one half, and one over

00:01:29.379 --> 00:01:31.123
minus two is minus a half.

00:01:32.027 --> 00:01:34.073
This mirrored curve is the natural log of

00:01:34.215 --> 00:01:34.916
minus x.

00:01:35.763 --> 00:01:36.894
The chain rule confirms it.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.167
Its derivative is one over minus x, times

00:01:40.208 --> 00:01:41.931
the inner derivative, minus one.

00:01:42.598 --> 00:01:43.367
That's one over x.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:45.299
Put the two pieces together.

00:01:45.702 --> 00:01:47.829
For positive x we have the natural log

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:48.251
of x,

00:01:48.753 --> 00:01:50.840
and for negative x, the natural log of

00:01:51.001 --> 00:01:51.603
minus x.

00:01:52.366 --> 00:01:54.674
Both are the natural log of mod x.

00:01:55.379 --> 00:01:56.970
Mod x is the size of x without

00:01:57.011 --> 00:01:57.393
its sign.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.506
Now watch the gradient as a point moves

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:01.449
along each piece.

00:02:02.114 --> 00:02:04.447
On both sides, it traces one over x

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:05.212
exactly.

00:02:05.696 --> 00:02:07.716
So the integral of one over x is

00:02:07.758 --> 00:02:10.438
the natural log of mod x, plus C,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.280
for x not equal to zero.

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:14.371
Notice the gap at zero.

00:02:14.936 --> 00:02:17.261
One over x isn't defined there, and mod

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:18.565
x doesn't fill the gap.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.608
So this primitive is two separate pieces.

00:02:22.352 --> 00:02:23.614
Slide the right piece up,

00:02:24.116 --> 00:02:25.439
and its gradients don't change.

00:02:26.222 --> 00:02:28.070
Slide the left piece down, and the same

00:02:28.091 --> 00:02:28.411
is true.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:32.001
Nothing joins the pieces across zero, so each

00:02:32.122 --> 00:02:33.645
one can have its own constant.

00:02:34.509 --> 00:02:36.820
Differentiate any of these curves, and you get

00:02:36.982 --> 00:02:38.328
one over x on each piece.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.179
In a question, you work on one piece

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.046
at a time, so you write the natural

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:44.531
log of mod x, plus C.

00:02:45.302 --> 00:02:46.549
Back to the waiting term.

00:02:47.192 --> 00:02:49.901
Four over x is four times one over

00:02:50.061 --> 00:02:50.182
x,

00:02:50.683 --> 00:02:52.991
so its integral is four times the natural

00:02:53.071 --> 00:02:54.255
log of mod x.

00:02:55.179 --> 00:02:57.452
Add the first term, and one constant for

00:02:57.472 --> 00:02:58.156
the whole answer.

00:02:58.699 --> 00:03:01.201
That's two thirds e to the three x,

00:03:01.621 --> 00:03:04.103
plus four times the natural log of mod

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:05.423
x, plus C,

00:03:05.984 --> 00:03:07.385
for x not equal to zero.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.193
Differentiate back to check.

00:03:09.777 --> 00:03:12.607
Two thirds times three gives two e to

00:03:12.628 --> 00:03:13.230
the three x,

00:03:13.733 --> 00:03:15.459
and four over x comes back.

00:03:16.125 --> 00:03:16.999
Back to the fundraiser.

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:20.196
Its total is a thousand times the natural

00:03:20.236 --> 00:03:21.723
log of t, plus C.

00:03:22.427 --> 00:03:25.101
Here t is positive, so no absolute value

00:03:25.161 --> 00:03:25.503
is needed.

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:29.032
After day one, two thousand dollars is in,

00:03:29.494 --> 00:03:31.558
and the natural log of one is zero,

00:03:32.019 --> 00:03:33.482
so C is two thousand.

00:03:34.525 --> 00:03:36.469
Each time the number of days doubles, it

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.954
grows by the same amount, about six hundred

00:03:38.975 --> 00:03:39.856
and ninety-three dollars.

00:03:40.559 --> 00:03:42.995
It never stops growing, but it keeps slowing

00:03:43.037 --> 00:03:43.257
down.

00:03:44.009 --> 00:03:45.736
Now a reciprocal with an inside.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.925
Find the integral of one over two x

00:03:49.127 --> 00:03:49.768
minus three.

00:03:50.651 --> 00:03:52.598
Try the natural log of mod two x

00:03:52.639 --> 00:03:53.160
minus three.

00:03:53.843 --> 00:03:56.071
By the chain rule, its derivative is two

00:03:56.273 --> 00:03:57.376
over two x minus three,

00:03:57.939 --> 00:03:58.762
twice what we want.

00:03:59.545 --> 00:04:01.608
On the graph, the log curve is squashed

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:04.294
sideways by a factor of two, then slid

00:04:04.335 --> 00:04:04.535
along.

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:07.603
The slide changes no slopes, but the squash

00:04:07.765 --> 00:04:08.666
doubles every one.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.755
It's the same cause as before, so divide

00:04:11.816 --> 00:04:12.598
by the inner rate.

00:04:13.281 --> 00:04:15.068
The answer is a half, times the natural

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:17.620
log of mod two x minus three, plus

00:04:17.761 --> 00:04:17.881
C.

00:04:18.729 --> 00:04:19.456
The gap moves too.

00:04:20.063 --> 00:04:21.968
Two x minus three is zero at x

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:23.333
equals three over two,

00:04:23.915 --> 00:04:25.520
so the answer works on either side of

00:04:25.561 --> 00:04:27.185
three over two, but not across it.

00:04:27.796 --> 00:04:29.830
What if the top isn't just a number?

00:04:30.575 --> 00:04:32.761
Find the integral of two x over x

00:04:32.782 --> 00:04:33.845
squared plus four.

00:04:34.592 --> 00:04:35.180
Look at the bottom.

00:04:35.809 --> 00:04:38.723
Its derivative is two x, which is exactly

00:04:38.765 --> 00:04:39.126
the top.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:41.753
By the chain rule, the natural log of

00:04:41.855 --> 00:04:44.580
mod f has derivative f prime over f.

00:04:45.222 --> 00:04:47.471
So this integral is the natural log of

00:04:47.552 --> 00:04:49.922
mod x squared plus four, plus C.

00:04:50.686 --> 00:04:52.955
Here, x squared plus four is at least

00:04:53.157 --> 00:04:54.884
four, so it's always positive.

00:04:55.407 --> 00:04:57.633
The absolute value can go, and the answer

00:04:57.654 --> 00:04:58.636
works for every x.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:01.422
But if the bottom were x squared minus

00:05:01.483 --> 00:05:04.066
four, it would change sign, so you'd keep

00:05:04.087 --> 00:05:06.550
the absolute value, with gaps at x equals

00:05:06.611 --> 00:05:07.832
two and minus two.

00:05:08.636 --> 00:05:09.661
One more from last video.

00:05:10.405 --> 00:05:12.466
Find the integral of e to the minus

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:15.970
x, plus three over x, plus x squared.

00:05:16.713 --> 00:05:19.228
Last video gave minus e to the minus

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:19.570
x.

00:05:20.335 --> 00:05:22.801
Three over x gives three times the natural

00:05:22.863 --> 00:05:23.985
log of mod x.

00:05:24.689 --> 00:05:27.146
And x squared gives x cubed over three.

00:05:27.892 --> 00:05:30.186
One plus C covers the lot, and x

00:05:30.248 --> 00:05:30.911
can't be zero.

00:05:31.536 --> 00:05:32.602
Here's the pattern to remember.

00:05:33.226 --> 00:05:34.827
When the top is the derivative of the

00:05:34.868 --> 00:05:37.471
bottom, the answer is the natural log of

00:05:37.632 --> 00:05:38.372
mod bottom.

00:05:39.034 --> 00:05:40.735
If the top is a constant multiple of

00:05:40.776 --> 00:05:42.697
that derivative, fix the number in front.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.908
And keep the absolute value, unless the bottom

00:05:45.949 --> 00:05:46.872
is always positive.

00:05:49.558 --> 00:05:50.024
Your turn.

00:05:50.487 --> 00:05:52.870
Find the integral of six over three x

00:05:52.912 --> 00:05:55.476
plus one, and state the values of x

00:05:55.597 --> 00:05:56.979
for which your answer is valid.

00:05:57.704 --> 00:05:58.611
Pause here to answer.

00:06:09.255 --> 00:06:11.844
The bottom, three x plus one, has derivative

00:06:11.986 --> 00:06:12.266
three,

00:06:12.809 --> 00:06:14.595
and six is two times three.

00:06:15.198 --> 00:06:17.388
So the answer is two times the natural

00:06:17.429 --> 00:06:19.819
log of mod three x plus one, plus

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:19.980
C.

00:06:21.063 --> 00:06:23.804
Differentiate back: two times three, over three x

00:06:23.825 --> 00:06:26.326
plus one, gives six over three x plus

00:06:26.447 --> 00:06:26.566
one.

00:06:27.328 --> 00:06:29.152
It's valid for x not equal to minus

00:06:29.214 --> 00:06:30.837
one third, on either side of it.

00:06:31.701 --> 00:06:33.430
Six times the log is wrong.

00:06:33.875 --> 00:06:35.711
It forgets to divide by the inner three.

00:06:37.388 --> 00:06:37.816
Last one.

00:06:38.422 --> 00:06:41.147
Find the integral of x squared over x

00:06:41.247 --> 00:06:42.449
cubed minus eight,

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:44.953
and state the values of x for which

00:06:45.014 --> 00:06:46.276
your answer is valid.

00:06:46.918 --> 00:06:47.854
Pause here to answer.

00:06:58.562 --> 00:07:01.214
The bottom's derivative is three x squared, and

00:07:01.234 --> 00:07:02.520
the top is a third of that.

00:07:03.183 --> 00:07:04.908
So the answer is a third of the

00:07:04.948 --> 00:07:07.635
natural log of mod x cubed minus eight,

00:07:07.996 --> 00:07:08.437
plus C.

00:07:09.279 --> 00:07:11.243
The bottom is zero when x is two,

00:07:11.684 --> 00:07:13.708
so the answer works for x less than

00:07:13.769 --> 00:07:15.773
two, or for x greater than two.

00:07:16.637 --> 00:07:18.424
Dropping the absolute value is wrong.

00:07:18.847 --> 00:07:20.190
For x less than two, x

00:07:20.792 --> 00:07:23.157
cubed minus eight is negative, and its log

00:07:23.239 --> 00:07:23.839
doesn't exist.

00:07:25.441 --> 00:07:27.887
So one over x integrates to the natural

00:07:27.927 --> 00:07:30.373
log of mod x, because the mirrored log

00:07:30.494 --> 00:07:31.576
covers the negative side.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:33.507
Next, the trig functions.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:35.458
Here's y equals sine x.

00:07:36.402 --> 00:07:39.025
Which curve has a gradient equal to sine

00:07:39.045 --> 00:07:39.986
x at every point?

00:07:40.808 --> 00:07:42.578
Is it cos x, or something else?

00:07:45.195 --> 00:07:46.058
Here are the key notes.

00:07:46.461 --> 00:07:48.008
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:48.511
to copy them.
